<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/dutch-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dutch%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dutch Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japan conquers the Netherlands East Indies in about three months</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/empire-of-japan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Empire%20of%20Japan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Empire of Japan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japan loses four fleet carriers at Midway, surrendering the strategic initiative</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-ecuador"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Ecuador.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Ecuador</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Rio Protocol assigns most of the disputed Amazon to Peru</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Commonwealth%20of%20Australia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Commonwealth of Australia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Singapore falls and Japanese aircraft bomb Darwin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/dutch-east-indies"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dutch%20East%20Indies.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dutch East Indies</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japan conquers the colony; the Dutch surrender on 8 March</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/british-raj"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/British%20Raj.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>British Raj</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Congress launches the Quit India movement</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/indian-independence-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Indian%20independence%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Indian independence movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Congress launches the Quit India Movement, and its leaders are imprisoned</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/navajo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Navajo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Navajo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Navajo transmitting Marine Corps combat simulations in their own language prove faster than any cryptographic facility, and the Marines recruit code talkers</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/mahatma-gandhi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mahatma%20Gandhi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mahatma Gandhi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He calls on the British to Quit India and is arrested and held for two years</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/independent-state-of-croatia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Independent%20State%20of%20Croatia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Independent State of Croatia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first formal agreement between Bosnian Chetniks and the Ustaše authorities is concluded</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/vichy-france"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vichy%20France.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vichy France</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">French police arrest 13,152 Jews in the Vel' d'Hiv Roundup</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/vichy-france"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vichy%20France.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vichy France</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Allies land in French North Africa and the Axis occupies southern France in Case Anton</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/vichy-france"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vichy%20France.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vichy France</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The French fleet is scuttled at Toulon to prevent its capture by the Axis</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/jawaharlal-nehru"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jawaharlal%20Nehru.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jawaharlal Nehru</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the Quit India resolution he is arrested with the Congress working committee</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-stalingrad"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Stalingrad.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Stalingrad</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Case Blue, the German summer offensive, opens on 28 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-stalingrad"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Stalingrad.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Stalingrad</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">German forces first clash with the Stalingrad Front on 17 July in the bend of the Don</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-stalingrad"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Stalingrad.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Stalingrad</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The 6th Army reaches the outskirts on 23 August and Luftflotte 4 bombs the city</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-stalingrad"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Stalingrad.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Stalingrad</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The battle for the city itself begins on 13 September</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-stalingrad"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Stalingrad.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Stalingrad</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 14 October a German assault reaches the Volga at the tractor factory and splits the 62nd Army</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-stalingrad"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Stalingrad.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Stalingrad</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Operation Uranus opens on 19 November and the ring closes at Kalach on 23 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-stalingrad"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Stalingrad.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Stalingrad</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Operation Winter Storm, the German relief attempt, is abandoned on 23 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-madagascar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Madagascar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Madagascar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japanese carrier raids on Ceylon drive the British Eastern Fleet to Kilindini, and Churchill agrees that planning for an invasion of Madagascar should begin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-madagascar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Madagascar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Madagascar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Operation Ironclad: British forces land at Courrier Bay and Ambararata Bay, west of Diego-Suarez</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-madagascar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Madagascar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Madagascar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Royal Marines landed from HMS Anthony break the Vichy defence at Antisarane, and Diego-Suarez falls</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-madagascar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Madagascar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Madagascar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japanese midget submarines damage HMS Ramillies and sink the tanker British Loyalty in Diego-Suarez harbour</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-madagascar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Madagascar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Madagascar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Operations Stream, Line and Jane: landings at Majunga and Tamatave, and Tananarive falls</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-madagascar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Madagascar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Madagascar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">King's African Rifles ambush Vichy troops at Andramanalina, and 800 surrender</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-madagascar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Madagascar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Madagascar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">An armistice is signed at Ambalavao, and Annet surrenders two days later</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-midway"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Midway.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Midway</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Yamamoto's plan to take Midway and destroy the American carriers is adopted after the Doolittle Raid on Tokyo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-midway"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Midway.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Midway</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">American code breakers confirm that the Japanese objective &quot;AF&quot; is Midway and give the attack date as 4 or 5 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-midway"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Midway.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Midway</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Midway-based aircraft find the Japanese occupation force, and the Japanese attack on the Aleutians begins</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-midway"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Midway.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Midway</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nagumo's aircraft bomb Midway at about 06:34, and American torpedo squadrons attack the carriers without success</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-midway"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Midway.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Midway</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">American dive bombers set Kaga, Sōryū and Akagi ablaze from 10:22</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-midway"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Midway.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Midway</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hiryū's two strikes cripple Yorktown, and in the afternoon American bombers leave Hiryū burning</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-midway"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Midway.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Midway</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Yamamoto orders a general withdrawal to the west</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-midway"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Midway.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Midway</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mikuma is sunk and Yorktown capsizes after submarine torpedoes</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-tarawa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Tarawa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Tarawa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Colonel Evans Carlson's raid on Makin Island makes the Japanese command aware of the vulnerability of the Gilbert Islands</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/fall-of-singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fall%20of%20Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fall of Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The last Commonwealth forces cross the causeway to Singapore on 31 January and engineers blow it up</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/fall-of-singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fall%20of%20Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fall of Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 8 February Japanese troops begin crossing the Johor Strait and land against the 22nd Australian Brigade</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/fall-of-singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fall%20of%20Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fall of Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Jurong Line collapses on 10 February and the Japanese take the Bukit Timah area the next day</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/fall-of-singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fall%20of%20Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fall of Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 15 February Percival surrenders to Yamashita at the Ford Motor Factory</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/fall-of-singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fall%20of%20Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fall of Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japan renames the city Syonan-to and murders thousands in the Sook Ching massacre</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/second-battle-of-el-alamein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Battle%20of%20El%20Alamein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Battle of El Alamein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Panzer Army Africa wins the Battle of Gazala and advances into Egypt</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/second-battle-of-el-alamein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Battle%20of%20El%20Alamein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Battle of El Alamein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Axis attacks in the First Battle of El Alamein are defeated</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/second-battle-of-el-alamein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Battle%20of%20El%20Alamein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Battle of El Alamein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Churchill and Brooke replace Auchinleck with Alexander, and Montgomery takes command of Eighth Army</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/second-battle-of-el-alamein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Battle%20of%20El%20Alamein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Battle of El Alamein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Operation Lightfoot opens with a barrage of 1,000 guns</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/second-battle-of-el-alamein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Battle%20of%20El%20Alamein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Battle of El Alamein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Operation Supercharge begins, and the 9th Armoured Brigade attacks the Axis gun line; on 4 November the Axis front is broken and Rommel orders a retreat</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/malacca"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Malacca.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Malacca</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japanese forces enter the city and occupy it until 1945</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/journey-to-the-west"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Journey%20to%20the%20West.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Journey to the West</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Arthur Waley publishes Monkey, an abridged English translation of 30 of the 100 chapters</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/quit-india-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Quit%20India%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Quit India movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Cripps Mission fails to win Congress support, and Gandhi calls its offer a post-dated cheque on a crashing bank</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/quit-india-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Quit%20India%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Quit India movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Congress working committee at Wardha adopts a resolution demanding complete independence on 14 July</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/quit-india-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Quit%20India%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Quit India movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gandhi delivers his Quit India speech at Bombay on 8 August, and almost the entire Congress leadership is imprisoned within hours</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/quit-india-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Quit%20India%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Quit India movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Between 9 August and 21 September protesters attack post offices, railway stations and police stations, and 57 battalions of British troops are deployed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/gandhism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Gandhism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Gandhism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Quit India Movement opens civil resistance against British rule</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/antisemitism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Antisemitism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Antisemitism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The mass murder by the Einsatzgruppen that began in 1941 culminates in the systematic genocide of the Holocaust</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/santeria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Santer%C3%ADa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Santería</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Rómula Lachatañeré's Manuel de santería is published, the first scholarly attempt to understand Santería as a religion</span></li></ul></section>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Wars and longer events</h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-stalingrad"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-stalingrad.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Battle of Stalingrad</span><span class="tp">Began · 1942–1943</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/guadalcanal-campaign"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guadalcanal-campaign.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Guadalcanal campaign</span><span class="tp">Began · 1942–1943</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manhattan-project"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manhattan-project.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manhattan Project</span><span class="tp">Began · 1942–1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/japanese-invasion-of-the-dutch-east-indies"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/japanese-invasion-of-the-dutch-east-indies.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Japanese invasion of the Dutch East Indies</span><span class="tp">Ended · 1941–1942</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
